ArchiveEntry "4-Machine CHAIN component-wise eps-delta Lyapunov stability (parametric in D1..D4,K)"

/*
 * KeYmaera X STATUS: NOT machine-verified (documented conjecture, no .kyp). The
 * 4-machine chain analog of lyapunov_complete_3machine. The MATH is sound; only
 * the Z3-only backend cannot close it at this dimension.
 *
 * Component-wise eps-delta stability of the passive chain, ALL D1..D4,K>0.
 * Witness delta = eps/(6K+4): from the box {w_i^2<delta (i=1..4), 1-c_j<delta
 * (j=1,2,3)} the energy is
 *   H = w1^2+w2^2+w3^2+w4^2+2K(1-c1)+2K(1-c2)+2K(1-c3)
 *     < 4*delta + 2K*3*delta = (6K+4)*delta = eps   (sympy: sup H = eps exactly),
 * H is invariant (dH/dt<=0), so each nonnegative energy component stays < eps.
 *
 * WHY OPEN HERE: the intended tactic is the SAME as the PROVED 3-machine version
 * (division-free witness cut \exists xd (xd>0 & (6K+4)*xd=eps); dC H<eps; dW; then
 * split the 7-conjunction post-condition into per-component QEs; dI). But the
 * 3-machine case has 10 ODE variables and the post-split QE is light; the
 * 4-machine case has 14 ODE variables + 3 circle constraints, and Z3 OOM-kills on
 * the dW;QE split (EXIT 137 at -Xmx4g; EXIT 124 timeout at -Xmx10g/600s). This is
 * the SAME high-dimension QE wall hit elsewhere -- a Mathematica/SOS backend (or a
 * QE that doesn't carry the full 14-var context into each leaf) would close it.
 *
 * Everything BELOW the eps-delta layer is machine-proven for the 4-machine chain:
 * H-metric Lyapunov (lyapunov_nonlinear_4machine), passive invariance
 * (parametric_4machine), conservation, energy identity. Only this component-form
 * eps-delta is left as a conjecture. Witness arithmetic checked exactly (sympy:
 * delta=eps/(6K+4) => sup H = eps). TOPOLOGY-INDEPENDENT in principle.
 *
 * (Per repo convention a conjecture carries Problem only, no Tactic. The intended
 * proof script is preserved in lyapunov_complete_3machine.kyx, which IS proved.)
 */

ProgramVariables
  Real da; Real db; Real dc; Real dd;
  Real w1; Real w2; Real w3; Real w4;
  Real s1; Real c1; Real s2; Real c2; Real s3; Real c3;
End.

Problem
  \forall D1 \forall D2 \forall D3 \forall D4 \forall K (
    D1 > 0 & D2 > 0 & D3 > 0 & D4 > 0 & K > 0 ->
    \forall eps (eps > 0 ->
      \exists delta (delta > 0 &
        \forall da \forall db \forall dc \forall dd \forall w1 \forall w2 \forall w3 \forall w4 \forall s1 \forall c1 \forall s2 \forall c2 \forall s3 \forall c3 (
          s1^2 + c1^2 = 1 & s2^2 + c2^2 = 1 & s3^2 + c3^2 = 1 &
          w1^2 < delta & w2^2 < delta & w3^2 < delta & w4^2 < delta &
          1 - c1 < delta & 1 - c2 < delta & 1 - c3 < delta
          ->
          [{da' = w1, db' = w2, dc' = w3, dd' = w4,
            w1' = -D1*w1 - K*s1,
            w2' = -D2*w2 + K*s1 - K*s2,
            w3' = -D3*w3 + K*s2 - K*s3,
            w4' = -D4*w4 + K*s3,
            s1' = c1*(w1 - w2), c1' = -s1*(w1 - w2),
            s2' = c2*(w2 - w3), c2' = -s2*(w2 - w3),
            s3' = c3*(w3 - w4), c3' = -s3*(w3 - w4)
            & s1^2 + c1^2 = 1 & s2^2 + c2^2 = 1 & s3^2 + c3^2 = 1}]
          (w1^2 < eps & w2^2 < eps & w3^2 < eps & w4^2 < eps &
           2*K*(1-c1) < eps & 2*K*(1-c2) < eps & 2*K*(1-c3) < eps)
        )
      )
    )
  )
End.

/*
 * No Tactic block: this is a documented conjecture (Problem only), per repo
 * convention. The intended proof is identical to lyapunov_complete_3machine.kyx
 * (division-free witness cut "(6*K+4)*xd = eps"; dC H<eps; dW; 7-way andR-split
 * QE; dI) but Z3 times out / OOMs on the 14-variable post-split QE here. See the
 * STATUS note at the top.
 */

End.
